{"id":"4eded96f-19fc-45a8-b549-5881279558e9","object":"chat.completion","created":1795147580,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"SELECT c.customer_state, ROUND(AVG(r.review_score), 2) AS avg_score\nFROM order_reviews r\nJOIN orders o ON o.order_id = r.order_id\nJOIN customers c ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id\nGROUP BY c.customer_state\nORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC, c.customer_state ASC\nLIMIT 10;","reasoning_content":"We need answer SQL only. Need parse Chinese: \"按订单客户档案所在州统计每条评价等权的平均分两位，按评价记录数取前10州，仅输出州和平均分，同数按州升序。\"\n\nNeed understand: average review score equally per review, grouped by state of order customer record, top 10 states by count of review records, only output state and average score, tie by state asc. Need include count for ordering but not select? In PostgreSQL can ORDER BY count DESC, state ASC without selecting count. Need two decimal average. Need join order_reviews -> orders -> customers. Average each review record equally, order_reviews PK (review_id,order_id), but rows are review records. Question \"每条评价等权\" means AVG(review_score) over review records. Join orders on order_id, customers on customer_id. Group by c.customer_state. ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC, c.customer_state ASC LIMIT 10. Output c.customer_state, ROUND(AVG(r.review_score),2). Need ensure AVG integer returns numeric? AVG(integer) returns numeric in PostgreSQL, ROUND okay. Could count duplicates? order_reviews one row per review_id/order_id, each evaluation record. \"按评价记录数\" likely COUNT(*) as rows. Need \"同数按州升序\". So ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC, c.customer_state ASC. Only select state and avg. LIMIT 10.\n\nNeed consider states null? c.customer_state could null? likely no, but if null state, ordering with ASC defaults NULLS LAST? PostgreSQL ASC default NULLS LAST. If \"同数按州升序\" maybe NULLS LAST default acceptable. Should we exclude null? No, not specified. We won't.\n\nNeed no code fence, directly SQL. Could include comment? User says only SQL, hard rule direct. No comment needed.\n\nNeed consider \"按订单客户档案所在州\": For each review, join to order then customer, use customer_state of order's customer record. yes.\n\nPotential issue: Multiple order_reviews per order? review_id, order_id primary means can have multiple rows per order? order_id not unique. \"每条评价等权\" count each review row. AVG review score over all rows. Fine.\n\nNeed only SELECT state and avg. Can ORDER BY count(*) though not selected. \"by review record count top 10\" yes.\n\nNeed maybe use COUNT(r.review_id) but since order_reviews join all non-null review_id? If review_id nullable? probably not. Use COUNT(*) as record count. In ORDER BY can use COUNT(*) DESC. Good.\n\nNeed state only. Should alias? maybe avg_score. Output state and average. SQL:\n\nSELECT c.customer_state, ROUND(AVG(r.review_score), 2) AS avg_score\nFROM order_reviews r\nJOIN orders o ON o.order_id = r.order_id\nJOIN customers c ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id\nGROUP BY c.customer_state\nORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC, c.customer_state ASC\nLIMIT 10;\n\nNeed \"两位\" two decimals. ROUND. yes.\n\nNeed maybe include c.customer_state as state? aliases okay. Only two columns. Good.\n\n final only SQL."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":3525,"completion_tokens":767,"total_tokens":4292,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":3328},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":686},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":3328,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":197},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}